ms.report:
Hey guys, Happy Holidays. This video shows that this API is working in order to have liquid democracies within DAOs on Cardano. There is not a public github link to this API because as mentioned in the proposals this proposal is not open source (https://projectcatalyst.io/funds/10/f10-daos-less3-cardano/clarity-dao-infrastructure-liquid-democracy-capability). We have released and revealed this API to our developers which you can see working in the demo video. We can invite you to the repo for you to check it out. 
The milestones purpose is to expose an API that our developers can use which has clearly happened since it is being used in the app.
For this PoA we have developed and implemented the necessary APIs and endpoints to enable seamless integration wit the front-end interface on testnet. The milestone is accomplished through a usable endpoint to accomplish stake delegation.
We have tested and validated the API functionality and ensured compatibility with the existing Clarity Protocol infrastructure. You can see the video as proof!
We have included the API documentation below as well!
Mainnet release soon!!!
Demo video of staking functionality on testnet: https://youtu.be/TDEXNZ9-drQ?si=WZWpjHUFRDmICryv
API Documentation: 
export declare function delegateStake(clarityParams: ClarityParams, stake: TransactionInput, delegateTo: Credential | null): Promise<TransactionHash>; 
API function to delegate Stake 
API Stake Datum to track who stakes are delegated to: 
export declare type StakeDatum = { 
stakedAmount: BigInteger; 
owner: Credential; 
delegatedTo: Credential | null; 
lockedBy: Array<ProposalLock>; }; 
function to get all stakes delegated to a wallet: export declare function getDelegatedStakes(clarityParams: ClarityParams): Promise<Array<ScriptUtxo<StakeDatum>>>;
